/-!
# Offenders on four-dimensional natural binary SL₃ extensions

For a faithful indecomposable binary four-space, an actual natural central
quotient identifies the best offenders with the full common-center groups.
An actual natural commutator submodule identifies them with the full
common-axis groups. Both families are quadratic and both ratios are one.
The fixed-space and Sylow conclusions concern the original action.
`earlierB48Two` and `earlierB48Three` discharge the complete universal inputs
of the literal B.5.9 and B.5.6 consumers, with the same actor marking.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, B.4.8(2)–(3), printed p.91 (1 March 2004).
-/
